{
  "note": [
    "The §3.1 masking table as data: which fields the vault renders masked, and",
    "therefore which ones fill_secret marks in the page.",
    "",
    "Two classifiers have to agree on it — the real one in",
    "vendor/browser-server/seed_vault_broker/cli.py (_field_descriptors) and the",
    "one in the JS fake broker that the python-free unit tier runs against. Each",
    "case therefore carries the SAME item twice: 'bitwarden' as the real vault",
    "stores it, 'fake' in the fake broker's vault format. 'expect' is the single",
    "source of truth both are asserted against, so a rule that drifts on one side",
    "fails rather than passing quietly.",
    "",
    "Entries with alias:true are the other names get-field accepts for a slot",
    "already listed (a card's code answers to cvv; a login's username to email).",
    "They carry the slot's own hidden flag, so no caller above the broker needs a",
    "copy of the mapping.",
    "",
    "",
    "Shapes and concealment come from the pinned Bitwarden client source, tag",
    "cli-v2026.7.0 (commit 82186c3d92c0da14aa86c848b781d949a8a6202a): item types",
    "in vault/enums/cipher-type.ts, identity keys in models/export/identity.export.ts,",
    "ssh key keys in models/export/ssh-key.export.ts, linked ids in",
    "vault/enums/linked-id-type.enum.ts, and what the client conceals in the",
    "cipher-view templates.",
    "",
    "",
    "Item types 6-8 (bank account, driving licence, passport) exist in the client",
    "but CANNOT be stored by the vault this app runs: vaultwarden 1.37.1",
    "(commit 2629bcbe1380c894e3a7f52cafcac3988edb8fbb) matches only types 1-5 in",
    "src/api/core/ciphers.rs:508-515 and answers anything else with",
    "err!(\"Invalid type\"). The three cases below pin that: an item of those types",
    "reports nothing, because one cannot get into the vault to be reported. When",
    "vaultwarden gains them, these are the cases to fill in.",
    "",
    "Consumed by packages/device-core/test/maskClassification.test.ts and",
    "e2e/fixtures/classifyProbe.py."
  ],
